  "limitations": "Three measured observations per binary, independent primers stabilized to two publications and loopback metadata service. One tiny fresh genrule per invocation forces both binaries to publish. Separate primers can differ in pack layout. Primers, stabilization and retained-chunk warmups excluded. Build-complete marker is output arrival, not exact method timing. Earlier attempts are excluded: an unpinned PATH changed the namespace; the rebuilt binary could not restore old analysis/execution keys; one candidate had no writes and skipped publication; and one baseline JVM crashed in compiled java.util.stream.Nodes$SpinedNodeBuilder.accept. Wall-clock steps occurred during this cohort, so no cross-clock pre-upload interval is reported; command and post-build intervals use the same monotonic clock. RPC durations are individual monotonic forwarding durations, not total publication latency. No WAN, percentile-latency or allocation claim."
